🌍 About the Company

Our client is a fully licensed EU bank based focused on providing modern banking infrastructure for FinTech companies, payment institutions, e-commerce businesses, and other digital-first companies
.
Combining traditional banking expertise with a FinTech-native approach, the bank provides solutions including Banking-as-a-Service (BaaS), e-commerce acquiring, payment infrastructure, safeguarding accounts, lending, and business banking services
.

💼 About the Role

As Head of IT Development / Engineering
, you will own the Bank's software engineering function and lead the development of secure, scalable, and reliable technology solutions that support its banking and FinTech products.
This senior leadership role combines engineering strategy, software architecture, delivery ownership, technology modernisation, and people leadership
. You will work closely with Product, Business, IT Operations, and other stakeholders to translate business needs into robust technical solutions while continuously strengthening engineering standards and practices.

🔍 Responsibilities

Own the end-to-end software development lifecycle
, including architecture, coding standards, code review practices, secure development, and technical debt management;
Lead the engineering delivery roadmap in close partnership with Product and Business stakeholders, translating business requirements into scalable technical solutions;
Own and continuously improve CI/CD pipelines and release engineering practices
, including build processes, automated testing, and deployment packaging through production handover;
Drive technology and platform modernization
, evaluating frameworks, programming languages, tools, and engineering practices;
Define and maintain high standards for application and integration quality
, including test coverage, defect management, code review discipline, and secure coding practices;
Establish effective processes for identifying, prioritizing, and reducing technical debt;
Ensure engineering solutions are designed with security, reliability, scalability, and maintainability
in mind, reflecting the requirements of a regulated banking environment;
Lead, mentor, and develop the engineering team, building a strong culture of ownership, collaboration, technical excellence, and continuous improvement
;
Take ownership of engineering talent management, including hiring, performance management, career development, and succession planning;
Collaborate closely with IT Operations and other technology stakeholders to ensure effective handover and reliable delivery into production.

🎓 Requirements

Strong experience in software engineering and technical leadership
, ideally within banking, FinTech, payments, or another regulated technology environment;
Proven experience leading software development teams and taking ownership of both people and engineering delivery
;
Strong understanding of software architecture, system design, integration patterns, and modern development practices
;
Hands-on understanding of CI/CD, automated testing, release engineering, and DevOps principles
;
Experience establishing and maintaining coding standards, code review processes, quality controls, and secure software development practices;
Experience driving technology modernization and technical debt reduction
in complex or business-critical environments;
Ability to translate business and product requirements into clear technical solutions and engineering priorities;
Strong understanding of software security and the expectations associated with developing systems in a regulated environment
;
Professional working proficiency in English
.

🤝 Key Competencies

Leadership & Ownership
- sets clear direction and builds accountability across engineering teams;
Technical Judgement
- makes pragmatic technology decisions balancing scalability, security, and business needs;
Strategic Thinking
- connects engineering priorities with wider business objectives;
Stakeholder Collaboration
- works effectively across Product, Business, IT Operations, and senior leadership.

✨ The Employer Offers

Modern office in the centre of Riga with a hybrid working model;
Opportunity to directly contribute to the Bank's technological development and future digital initiatives;
Dynamic working environment with a supportive management team that values innovation;
Collaborative, supportive, and innovation-driven working environment;
Monthly salary €5,500 - €6,000 ;
Health insurance after the probation period;
Long-term career growth within a stable organisation committed to continuous technological development.

If you want to lead more than a development team, this role gives you the ownership to shape engineering standards, technology direction, and the platforms behind a growing FinTech bank.

Show more

Show less

Seniority level

Not Applicable

Employment type

Full-time

Job function

Engineering, Information Technology, and Business Development

Industries

Financial Services

🌍 About the Company

Our client is a fully licensed EU bank that provides modern banking infrastructure for FinTech companies, payment institutions, e-commerce businesses, and other digital-first companies
.
Combining traditional banking expertise with a FinTech-native approach, the bank provides solutions including Banking-as-a-Service (BaaS), e-commerce acquiring, payment infrastructure, safeguarding accounts, lending, and business banking services
.

💼 About the Role

As Head of IT Operations
, you will own the Bank's production infrastructure, IT service management, operational resilience, and end-user technology environment.
In a highly regulated banking environment, you will ensure critical technology services remain secure, available, resilient, and compliant
. The role combines infrastructure leadership, IT operations, cybersecurity controls, business continuity, vendor management, and regulatory engagement.
You will work closely with Engineering, Information Security, Risk, Compliance, and business stakeholders to ensure the Bank's technology environment can reliably support its continued growth.

🔍 Responsibilities

Own the Bank's production infrastructure
, including servers, networks, cloud and on-premise environments, infrastructure architecture, and capacity planning;
Lead IT Service Management (ITSM)
processes, including incident, problem, and change management in line with ITIL principles;
Establish and maintain effective on-call, escalation, and major incident management
structures;
Own system reliability and operational resilience, including monitoring, alerting, disaster recovery, business continuity planning, and regular testing
;
Take responsibility for infrastructure and operational security controls, including patch management, vulnerability management, access controls, and infrastructure hardening
;
Ensure IT operations meet relevant banking, regulatory, audit, and ICT risk requirements
, including DORA and applicable local regulatory requirements;
Coordinate IT-related regulatory and audit activities, including communication with auditors and regulators, evidence collection, remediation planning, and implementation of corrective actions;
Manage relationships with infrastructure, data centre, cloud, software, and licensing vendors
, ensuring appropriate service levels, controls, and commercial oversight;
Own end-user IT services, including helpdesk, workplace technology, device management, and employee IT support
;
Define and monitor operational performance and service availability through relevant SLAs, KPIs, and operational metrics;
Partner closely with Engineering and other technology teams to ensure controlled and reliable production deployments and ongoing system stability;
Lead and continuously improve IT operational processes, documentation, controls, and ways of working.

🎓 Requirements

Strong experience in IT infrastructure and operations leadership
, ideally within banking, financial services, FinTech, payments, or another highly regulated environment;
Proven experience managing business-critical production environments
across cloud and/or on-premise infrastructure;
Strong knowledge of IT Service Management and ITIL-aligned practices
, particularly incident, problem, and change management;
Solid understanding of networking, servers, cloud infrastructure, monitoring, capacity planning, and operational security
;
Hands-on experience with disaster recovery, business continuity, operational resilience, and recovery testing
;
Strong understanding of infrastructure security controls, including patching, vulnerability management, identity/access management, and security remediation;
Experience working with IT audits, regulatory requirements, and evidence-based technology controls
;
Knowledge of ICT risk and regulatory frameworks relevant to EU financial institutions, including DORA
, would be highly valuable;
Experience managing technology vendors, third-party providers, contracts, and service levels;
Strong stakeholder management skills with the ability to work effectively across Engineering, Security, Risk, Compliance, Audit, and senior leadership;
Professional working proficiency in English
.

🤝 Key Competencies

Operational Ownership
- takes responsibility for stable, secure, and reliable technology services;
Risk & Resilience Mindset
- balances operational performance with security, regulatory, and business continuity requirements;
Leadership & Decision-Making
- creates accountability and stays decisive during critical situations;
Stakeholder Collaboration
- works confidently across Engineering, Security, Risk, Compliance, auditors, and external partners.

✨ The Employer Offers

Modern office in the centre of Riga with a hybrid working model;
Opportunity to directly contribute to the Bank's technological development and future digital initiatives;
Dynamic working environment with a supportive management team that values innovation;
Collaborative, supportive, and innovation-driven working environment;
Monthly salary €5,500 - €6,000;
Health insurance after the probation period;
Long-term career growth within a stable organisation committed to continuous technological development.

If you know how to keep critical technology secure, resilient, and reliable while navigating the demands of a regulated banking environment, this role gives you the ownership to shape IT operations where technology performance directly impacts the business.

Show more

Show less

Seniority level

Not Applicable

Employment type

Full-time

Job function

Information Technology

Industries

Financial Services

